          %h2#parameterized_pointset_topology Parameterized point-set topology
          %blockquote
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
              of parametrized spaces is surprisingly subtle. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#MaySigurdsson06"}> May &amp; Sigurdsson 2006, p. 15
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Write:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi kTop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} kTop
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
                (k-spaces)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi kwHaus
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} kwHaus \subset Top_k
                for that of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+weak+Hausdorff+spaces"} compactly generated weak Hausdorff spaces
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \,\in\, \mathcal{C}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/B}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            over it.
          %p
            In the following all bases spaces are assumed (as in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MaySigurdsson06"} MaSi06, p. 19
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+weak+Hausdorff+spaces"} compactly generated weak Hausdorff spaces
            regarded among k-spaces:
          #eq:kwHausBaseSpace.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
